@sen1158    It has been both asserted and denied that the American cuckoo occasionally lays her eggs in other birds' nests; but I have lately heard from Dr Merrill, of Iowa, that he once found in Illinois a young cuckoo, together with a young jay in the nest of a blue jay Garrulus cristatus; and as both were nearly full feathered, there could be no mistake in their identification. I could also give several instances of various birds which have been known occasionally to lay their eggs in other birds' nests.

