@sen1370    It is generally different, and sometimes widely different in reciprocal crosses between the same two species.

              " (extract-fr) part 30 of Darwin about: other hand, each other, natural selection, intermediate varieties, geological record, two species, transitional links, from each other, any two species

@sen1371    It is not always equal in degree in a first cross and in the hybrids produced from this cross.

