@sen1632     Groups of species, that is, genera and families, follow the same general rules in their appearance and disappearance as do single species, changing more or less quickly, and in a greater or lesser degree.

              " (extract-fr) part 36 of Darwin about: south america, natural selection, north america, different climates, extinct species, other mammals, tertiary formations, large sense, throughout the world, forms of life, varieties and species, groups of species, most different climates, rich in fossils, from the world

@sen1636    For all the species of the same group, however long it may have lasted, are the modified descendants one from the other, and all from a common progenitor.

